# Canonical input for requirements/locks/web-<platform>-x86_64.txt.
# Regenerate with pip-tools==7.6.1 on the target platform (see requirements/README.md):
# python -m piptools compile --allow-unsafe --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements/locks/web-linux-x86_64.txt --strip-extras requirements/web.in
# python -m piptools compile --allow-unsafe --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements/locks/web-macos-x86_64.txt --strip-extras requirements/web.in
# python -m piptools compile --allow-unsafe --generate-hashes --output-file=requirements/locks/web-windows-x86_64.txt --strip-extras requirements/web.in
#
# The isolated `comic-sol-web` distribution (see web/pyproject.toml). Direct
# pins are restricted to the Web architecture named in umbrella issue #251:
# FastAPI, Uvicorn, HTTPX, Authlib, cryptography, and python-multipart, plus
# the Web distribution's own required build and quality tools so its CI can
# install and test it without resolving uncontrolled dependencies. No provider
# SDKs, databases, frontend build systems, telemetry, or hosted service
# clients are added here. pip is pinned explicitly so the interpreter that
# later performs --require-hashes installs is itself hash-verified.
